    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"applied cognitive engineering\"... that sounds so much more sinister when you put it that way. if they're using fractal geometry and specific ratios to create an \"automatic\" response, then it's not even about convincing us to buy something anymore, is it? it’s more like they're hijacking the brain's processing. \n\nit makes me wonder how widespread this actually is. if these patterns are being calculated to bypass our rational decision-making, do you think there's a threshold where this stops being \"marketing\" and starts being a form of mass psychological manipulation or even a coordinated effort to control consumer behavior through neural triggers?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
